# {{APP_NAME}} Mobile — Project Guide

## Stack

{{#if expo}}
Expo prebuild workflow on React Native {{RN_VERSION}} (New Architecture only), bundle id `{{BUNDLE_ID}}`, TypeScript strict.
{{else}}
Bare React Native {{RN_VERSION}} (New Architecture only), bundle id `{{BUNDLE_ID}}`, TypeScript strict.
{{/if}}
{{#if expoRouter}}
Navigation: expo-router (file routes in `app/`).
{{else}}
Navigation: @react-navigation (native-stack + bottom-tabs). `NavigationRoot` owns the `NavigationContainer`, theme and linking; `RootNavigator` switches Auth / App by session.
{{/if}}
{{#if rtk}}
State: Redux Toolkit (`src/store/`: slices, listeners, selectors) with RTK Query for server data (`src/store/api/`, one file per resource).
{{/if}}
{{#if zustand}}
State: zustand stores in `src/store/`.
{{/if}}
{{#if noState}}
State: React state + context only.
{{/if}}
{{#if tanstack}}
Server data: TanStack Query (`QueryClientProvider` in `src/app/Providers.tsx`).
{{/if}}
{{#if plainFetch}}
Server data: typed `fetch` wrapper in `src/lib/api.ts`.
{{/if}}
{{#if nativewind}}
Styling: NativeWind 4 + Tailwind 3 (`tailwind.config.js` reads `src/theme/tokens`, `global.css` is the entry).
{{/if}}
{{#if unistyles}}
Styling: react-native-unistyles 3 (babel plugin rooted at `src/`, themes in `src/theme/`).
{{/if}}
{{#if stylesheet}}
Styling: plain `StyleSheet` with tokens from `src/theme/`.
{{/if}}
{{#if mmkv}}
Storage: react-native-mmkv 4 (`src/lib/storage/`, two instances `{{APP_SLUG}}.auth` and `{{APP_SLUG}}.default`); no redux-persist, persistence is a listener.
{{/if}}
{{#if asyncStorage}}
Storage: @react-native-async-storage (`src/lib/storage/`); persistence is explicit, no redux-persist.
{{/if}}
{{#if noStorage}}
Storage: none yet — add mmkv via `src/lib/storage/` when the first persisted value arrives.
{{/if}}
{{#if rhf}}
Forms: react-hook-form + @hookform/resolvers + zod 4 (schemas in `src/validations/`).
{{/if}}
{{#if i18n}}
i18n: i18next + react-i18next + react-native-localize; every string is a key in `src/i18n/locales/en.json` — no inline strings.
{{/if}}
{{#if flashList}}
Lists: @shopify/flash-list 2 (no `estimatedItemSize`; masonry is a prop).
{{/if}}
Always on: reanimated 4 + worklets, gesture-handler 3, safe-area-context, react-native-svg, keyboard-controller, date-fns, es-toolkit.
{{#if crash}}
Crash reporting: @sentry/react-native, initialised in `src/app/` before the first render (DSN from `.env`).
{{/if}}
{{#if analytics}}
Analytics: facade in `src/lib/analytics.ts` with a no-op driver — swap the vendor without touching call sites.
{{/if}}
{{#if push}}
Push: @react-native-firebase/app + messaging (modular API) + react-native-permissions; background handler registered in `index.js`.
{{/if}}
{{#if media}}
Media: react-native-image-picker + react-native-video 6.
{{/if}}
{{#if roles}}
Roles: capability gating via `src/lib/roles` — gate on capabilities, never on role names, in screens.
{{/if}}

### Version pairing rules

- JS-only deps float carets; native modules are exact pins in `package.json`. Add a one-line "why" here for every pin that deviates from the resolver's choice.
- Paired packages move together, never one side alone:
  - reanimated ↔ worklets ↔ RN (check swmansion's compatibility table on every bump; floor 4.5.0, never 4.4.x)
{{#if rhf}}
  - zod ↔ @hookform/resolvers ↔ react-hook-form
{{/if}}
{{#if i18n}}
  - i18next ↔ react-i18next
{{/if}}
{{#if mmkv}}
  - react-native-nitro-modules ↔ react-native-mmkv
{{/if}}
{{#if unistyles}}
  - react-native-nitro-modules ↔ react-native-unistyles
{{/if}}
{{#if push}}
  - @react-native-firebase/app ↔ @react-native-firebase/messaging
{{/if}}
{{#if nativewind}}
- Tailwind stays on 3.x (`~` range). NativeWind 4's peer range admits Tailwind 4, which breaks the build.
{{/if}}
- Every native bump: changelog + New-Arch check (reactnative.directory) + full native rebuild + on-device test on both platforms.
- `@testing-library/react-native` v14 pairs with the npm package `test-renderer` (not `react-test-renderer`); `render`/`fireEvent`/`act` are async — await them.

Add-ons chosen at kickstart: {{ADDONS_LIST}}. Each is a native module with an exact pin; add a jest stub in `jest/` the day you import one in a tested file.

## Running the app

- Node from `.nvmrc` (`nvm use`), package manager: `{{PM}}`.
{{#if expo}}
- `{{PM}} run prebuild` generates `ios/` and `android/`; `{{PM}} run ios` / `{{PM}} run android` build and launch; `{{PM}} run start` for Metro only.
- `APP_VARIANT=development|staging|production` (per profile in `eas.json`, read by `app.config.ts`) decides name and bundle id. Runtime values come from `.env.development` / `.env.production` as `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variables, which Expo CLI inlines into the bundle by `NODE_ENV`; `src/config/env.ts` is the only reader. Keep both files committed so EAS can read them.
{{else}}
- `{{PM}} run pods` (Bundler-managed CocoaPods), then `{{PM}} run ios` / `{{PM}} run android`; `{{PM}} run start` for Metro only.
- Two environments: `{{BUNDLE_ID}}.dev` (Android `dev` flavor / iOS Debug → `.env.development`) and `{{BUNDLE_ID}}` (`prod` flavor / iOS Release → `.env.production`). react-native-config bakes the file in at build time; each flavor applies its own file in `android/app/build.gradle`, and the Podfile maps `ENVFILE` per Xcode configuration. `src/config/env.ts` is the only reader. Editing an env file needs a native rebuild; Metro reload will not pick it up. No `API_BASE_URL` literals elsewhere.
{{/if}}
- **Done gate:** `{{PM}} run verify` (typecheck + lint + jest) must be green before any task is called done. CI runs the same on every PR.
{{#if sample}}
- E2E smoke: `maestro test .maestro/login.yaml` against a Debug build on a simulator.
{{/if}}

